Author: loop-bench <loop-bench@localhost>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 09:28:00 2026 +0100

    feat(transport): answer list_sessions with session_list off the lock

    Thread the session store into createMessageHandler (optional second
    parameter) and answer list_sessions on the non-locked path beside ping:
    listFor runs with the socket's authenticated session.userId, any client
    userId already stripped by the validator, and the summaries go out as
    ISO strings via sendSessionList. A store without listFor answers an
    empty list; one that fails is logged on the ws category with the
    session id and answered SERVER_ERROR with its message kept off the wire.

    Also clears the lint findings CI named on the last push: the frame
    validator dispatches through a Map instead of a three-way switch, the
    limit check is a named predicate, and the duplicated test scaffolding
    (teardown, delegating store, malformed frames) now lives once in
    wsTestSupport. CHANGELOG carries the Unreleased entry the changelog
    gate asked for, and spec anchors are repointed to the moved tests.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

